# The zcrypto CLI's own Grafana Cloud Loki push credentials (spec 00068 D5), rendered by the
# `ops` role from group_vars/observed/vault.yml -- do not hand-edit on the host, it is overwritten
# on the next converge. Consumed by the ops-node LIQUIDATIONS CONTAINER's `--ship-logs` path
# (compose.yaml.j2's `env_file`), NOT by Alloy -- see alloy-secrets.env.j2 for Alloy's own copy, a
# distinct token so the app's push can be revoked without blinding fleet telemetry.
# Only ZCRYPTO_LOKI_PASSWORD is a distinct credential (logship_loki_token, access policy
# `zcrypto-app-logship`, scope logs:write only): the URL and USERNAME are properties of the
# Grafana Cloud stack, not of the token, so they are reused from grafana_loki_url /
# grafana_loki_user -- the same values alloy-secrets.env.j2 renders. One value to rotate, nothing
# to drift.
# Names must match cli/__main__.py's `_LOKI_ENV_NAMES` exactly -- env_file passes them straight
# through with no translation, so a rename here silently breaks --ship-logs with no test to catch it.
ZCRYPTO_LOKI_URL={{ grafana_loki_url }}
ZCRYPTO_LOKI_USERNAME={{ grafana_loki_user }}
ZCRYPTO_LOKI_PASSWORD={{ logship_loki_token }}
# ZCRYPTO_SHIP_LOGS lives HERE for schema parity with the capture role's copy (00068 T4/T5 review
# Minor-1) -- but on THIS host the CLI's --ship-logs flag is baked directly into the liquidations
# service's exec-form entrypoint (compose.yaml.j2), never read from this var: an exec-form
# `entrypoint:` override replaces the image's shell ENTRYPOINT wholesale, so the Dockerfile's
# `${ZCRYPTO_SHIP_LOGS:+--ship-logs}` conveyance never runs for this service. This line is
# therefore inert here (harmless, unread) -- kept only so every logship-secrets.env.j2 in the
# fleet shares one schema. Residual worth knowing: if this file goes missing after a converge
# (compose's env_file `required: false`), the other four vars disappear too, but the entrypoint's
# --ship-logs stays baked in regardless -- so the CLI still raises BadParameter on the missing
# creds and crash-loops. Unlike capture, this host's entrypoint cannot self-heal to no-ship-logs
# at runtime; `required: false` only keeps `docker compose up` itself from refusing to start.
ZCRYPTO_SHIP_LOGS=1
